    common: add lockfiles for cache ops
    
    when using a shared DL_DIR across build, e.g. multiple
    machines with NFS shared DL_DIR, or even multiconfig builds,
    it could happen that one machine is running do_archive_pub_cache
    (recreating/updating the cache file), while another runs do_restore_pub_cache.
    This creates a race condition, where randomly do_restore_pub_cache
    would fail wil an UnpackError.
    To work around this issue, use a shared lock file for the cache artifact across
    all tasks using it.
    
    Signed-off-by: Konrad Weihmann <konrad.weihmann@avnet.eu>

